# Frontend Conventions

## Imports

- ES imports only — NEVER `require()`
- Use `@/lib/store` for Zustand state
- Use `@/lib/api` for REST calls — never raw `fetch()` with relative URLs
- Use `@/lib/ws` for WebSocket connection

## State management

- Zustand store in `lib/store.ts` — single source of truth
- WebSocket events update store; components subscribe reactively
- Demo mode in `lib/demo.ts` — generates synthetic events when backend is offline

## Styling

- CSS variables defined in `globals.css` (--bg, --surface, --accent, --text, etc.)
- Inline `style={{}}` for dynamic theming — not Tailwind classes for colors
- Tailwind for layout, spacing, typography
- Badge classes: `.badge-vip`, `.badge-staff`, `.badge-regular`, `.badge-new`

## Components

- All dashboard components in `components/dashboard/`
- ErrorBoundary wraps main content area
- HealthPanel polls `/health/detail` every 10 seconds
- ChatDrawer uses both WebSocket and REST API fallback

## API URLs

- Always use env vars: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL`
- Localhost fallbacks only for local dev
